2. Text Preprocessing

Prepares raw text for analysis.

a) Tokenization

Splits text into words or sentences.

Example:

Artificial Intelligence is amazing.

Word Tokens:

Artificial
Intelligence
is
amazing

Sentence Tokens:

Artificial Intelligence is amazing.
AI is the future.

Python:

word_tokenize()
sent_tokenize()
b) Lowercasing
AI → ai
Robot → robot
c) Removing Punctuation

Before:

Hello!

After:

Hello
d) Stop Word Removal

Removes common words.

Example:

is
the
a
an
of
to

Python:

stopwords.words("english")
e) Stemming

Converts words to their root.

Examples:

playing → play
studies → studi
walking → walk

Python:

PorterStemmer()
f) Lemmatization

Produces dictionary words.

Examples:

running → run
better → good
studies → study

Python:

WordNetLemmatizer()
3. Part-of-Speech (POS) Tagging

Identifies grammatical roles.

Example:

Robot is intelligent

Output:

Robot        Noun
is           Verb
intelligent  Adjective

Python:

pos_tag()
4. Named Entity Recognition (NER)

Finds names of people, places, organizations, etc.

Example:

Sundar Pichai works at Google.

Output:

Sundar Pichai → Person
Google → Organization
5. Text Representation

Converts text into numbers.

Bag of Words (BoW)

Counts word frequency.

TF-IDF

Measures word importance.

Python:

TfidfVectorizer()
